Maps: every world outline is drawn in marker by this project from open boundary data johan/world.geo.json (public domain,
Natural Earth 110m): coastlines = country edges not shared by two countries (scenes/geo.py), simplified (Douglas–Peucker).
  Mercator, Gall–Peters (equal-area cylindrical), Winkel tripel, orthographic globe centred on 15°W 30°N; Tissot circles
  (7° radius) on the three flat maps; Greenland dragged to the equator = rigid rotation on the sphere, then Mercator (true size).
  The project's own pre-made map images (cs_*, gall_peters_map, winkel_tripel_map ...) are not used. No generated images.

